  "category": "moving_head_wash",
  "description": "The Clay Paky HY B-EYE K25 is a single cylindrical moving-head wash fixture, probably 41 by 50 by 35 cm. A flat base plinth carries a U-shaped yoke arm that holds the head on a tilt axle. Pan turns the yoke and head through 540 degrees, and tilt swings the head 210 degrees (-105 to 105) inside the yoke, both DMX driven. A flat lens disc with a zoom housing behind it fills the circular front bezel. Thirty-seven hexagonal RGBW lens cells form a honeycomb about seven rows deep, with rows of 4 to 7 cells separated by thin black dividers. Each cell is probably independently controllable in red, green, blue and white. Lens rotation is probably unmodelled.",
